    "repo": "swesmith/rubik__radon.54b88e58",
    "problem_statement": "CCHarvester.as_xml() method calls non-existent _to_dict() instead of _to_dicts()\n\n#### Description\n\nThe `as_xml()` method in `CCHarvester` class is calling `_to_dict()` which doesn't exist, instead of the correct `_to_dicts()` method.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom radon.cli import harvest\nfrom radon.complexity import cc_visit\n\n# Create a CCHarvester instance\nconfig = {'min': 'A', 'max': 'F', 'show_complexity': True, 'average': False, 'order': 'SCORE'}\nharvester = harvest.CCHarvester([], config)\n\n# Try to call as_xml() method\ntry:\n    result = harvester.as_xml()\n    print(\"XML output:\", result)\nexcept AttributeError as e:\n    print(\"Error:\", e)\n```\n\nThis will raise an `AttributeError` because `_to_dict()` method doesn't exist on the `CCHarvester` class. The method should be calling `_to_dicts()` instead."
  }
}
